From c3a573e92bacd13f431010782500c4283ae09970 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:54:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mod menus: the game's own mod messages reach the client
 again; item menus tick with their player

Two bugs left the strings of mod menus blank (text widgets with text_data):

1. The game's own messages on the mod payload (horizon:menu_text, horizon:menu_grid, horizon:hud_line,
   horizon:radial to the client; horizon:key and horizon:grid_click to the server) went through the mods'
   send path, whose channel check refuses the horizon namespace: every one was dropped in silence. They now
   go through native_net_send_game / native_net_send_game_to_server (mod_net::game_channel_ok); mods still
   cannot use horizon:, and a client's horizon: channels other than key and grid_click never reach the mods.
2. During the mods' tick self.mods.players was taken out (mem::take) while tick_item_menus and the entity
   menu takes looked the player up there, so no item menu ever ticked. It is now replaced by this tick's
   players instead.

Also: an item menu's title is menu.<ns>.<name> only when the language has it, else the item's name; ui
reports an open mod menu's text widgets as drawn (menu_texts); horizon-ctl key takes backslash.
Test: agent_control_e2e.py --scenario mod-menu opens item-menu-demo's menu by its key and checks the strings
from its server reach the client and follow the hand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
